{"name":"Lush","hex":"#c5bda0","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Lush","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Lush"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lush (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Lush were an English rock band formed in London in 1987. The original line-up consisted of Miki Berenyi, Emma Anderson, Steve Rippon and Chris Acland (drums). Phil King replaced Rippon in 1991. They were one of the first bands to have been described with the \"shoegaze\" label. Following the death of Acland, the group disbanded in 1996."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Lush_pale_saint_2Mo.jpg/330px-Lush_pale_saint_2Mo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lush_(band)","wikidata":"Q1668512"},{"title":"Lush (Mitski album)","blocks":[{"text":"Lush is the debut studio album by American musician Mitski. Mitski self-released the album on January 31, 2012, as her junior year project at SUNY Purchase's Conservatory of Music. It was recorded and mixed by Scot Moriarty."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/c5/Lush_album_cover_%28Mitski%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lush_(Mitski_album)","wikidata":"Q104843276"},{"title":"Lush (company)","blocks":[{"text":"Lush Ltd. is a British cosmetics retailer which is headquartered in Poole, England. It was founded in 1995 by trichologist Mark Constantine, his wife Mo Constantine and five other founders."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Lush%2C_Lands_Lane%2C_Leeds_%281st_February_2020%29.jpg/330px-Lush%2C_Lands_Lane%2C_Leeds_%281st_February_2020%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lush_(company)","wikidata":"Q1585448"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://t